  "summary_en": "Binding Civil Aviation Directive issued by CAAM under the Civil Aviation Act 1969, setting the approval process and requirements for Special UAS Project operations (BVLOS, carriage of items and dangerous goods, R&D). It uses SORA/PDRA risk assessment, SAIL levels, safety management, UTM services, insurance, and oversight.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "No person may conduct Special UAS Project operations without a valid CAAM SUP Approval, valid up to one year.",
   "Applications must be based on a SORA or PDRA operational risk assessment; SAIL III and above requires all five certification phases.",
   "UAS operators must maintain third-party liability insurance and a management system with Accountable Manager, Safety Manager, FOM and ATP.",
   "Operators must provide UTM services, remote pilot training/currency, occurrence reporting and quarterly end reports.",
   "Contraventions are offences under section 24O of the Civil Aviation Act 1969; PDPA 2010 applies to imagery of identifiable individuals."
  ],
